  "genanki_title": "genanki library not installed",
  "genanki_msg": ".apkg export needs the genanki library.\n\nInstall with:  pip install genanki\n\nMeanwhile, use \"Export .txt\".",
  "apkg_err_title": "Error creating .apkg",
  "help_title": "Help — EasyAnkiCards v{v}",
  "help_close": "Close",
  "prompt_full_btn": "Copy full prompt",
  "prompt_mini_btn": "Copy short prompt (Gemini Notebook)",
  "copied": "Copied!",
  "example": "# Example — delete these lines and paste your content.\n# Format:  Front :: Back :: tags (tags are optional)\n# Tip: leave a blank line between cards.\nWhat is the principle of tax anteriority? :: Rule forbidding tax collection in the same fiscal year as the law that created it. :: tax\n\nWhat is the speed of light? :: About 300,000 km/s. :: physics\n\nThe capital of France is {{c1::Paris}}. :: Basic geography :: geography\n",
  "prompt_full": "Create Anki flashcards from the text I will send at the end.\n\nFORMAT RULES (follow exactly):\n1. One card per line, with a BLANK LINE between cards.\n2. Format: Question :: Answer :: tags\n   - Separate fields with \" :: \" (double colon).\n   - Tags: optional, 1-3 lowercase words without spaces (use _), comma-separated.\n3. Cloze cards: wrap the term to memorize in {{c1::term}}. Each blank in the SAME card uses a DIFFERENT number (c1, c2, c3) — never repeat a number within one card. The 2nd field becomes an optional note.\n4. NEVER use \"::\" inside the text (only as separator and inside {{c1::...}}).\n5. Each card must be short, self-contained, and test ONE single idea.\n6. Reply ONLY with the cards: no numbering, bullets or comments.\n7. MULTIPLE CHOICE questions — use one of these two forms:\n   a) Option list (mark the correct one with *):\n      [MC] Question? :: option | correct option * | option :: explanation :: tags\n   b) Inside the sentence (blank with options, the correct one repeated among them):\n      The capital of France is {{c1::Paris::Lyon / Paris / Marseille}}. :: note :: tags\n      IMPORTANT: only use form (b) with SHORT options (up to 40 characters each).\n      Anki prints all options in brackets on the same line; with long sentences the\n      card becomes unreadable. For long options, always use form (a).\n\n8. EXTRA EXPLANATION (optional, very useful): right below a card, add a line starting with \"+\" (the app also accepts \"*\") containing an explanation reviewing the topic in 3 to 15 lines, covering the context, the general rule and a practical example. For readability: one concept per \"+\" line, starting with the key term followed by \" — \", and \"+ ---\" to separate blocks. Example:\nWhat is the writ of mandamus deadline? :: 120 days :: mandamus\n+ It is a decadential deadline counted from awareness of the challenged act. It is neither interrupted nor suspended, and its expiry does not bar ordinary remedies.\n\n9. TITLE (optional): to print a title at the top of the card (subject or topic), use a line JUST FOR IT, starting with \"@\", immediately ABOVE the card. The title must NEVER share the line with the card.\n   WRONG:  @ Semantics - Paraphrase What is paraphrase? :: ...\n   RIGHT:  @ Semantics - Paraphrase\n           What is paraphrase? :: ...\n   Another example:\nWhat is the writ of mandamus deadline? :: 120 days :: mandamus\n@ Constitutional Law\n\nOUTPUT EXAMPLE:\nWhat is the speed of light? :: About 300,000 km/s. :: physics\n\nThe capital of France is {{c1::Paris}}. :: Basic geography :: geography\n\nSOURCE TEXT:\n[paste your study material here]\n10. One card per line: the WHOLE answer on the SAME line as the question — to list items use \" / \" (answer line ONLY, never inside \"+\" lines) or \"<br>\", never split across lines. No markdown (**bold**, ##); to emphasize, <b>text</b>.",
  "prompt_mini": "Create flashcards from the sources. Required format: one card per line, blank line between cards, pattern \"Question :: Answer :: tags\". For blanks use {{c1::term}}. Never use \"::\" inside the text. Short cards, one idea each. Multiple choice: \"[MC] Question? :: opt | correct opt * | opt :: explanation\" or {{c1::correct::option / option / correct}} (the latter only with short options, up to 40 characters). Reply only with the cards, no numbering or comments. If useful, add a line below the card starting with \"+\" explaining the topic in 3 to 15 lines, with context, general rule and an example. For a title at the top of the card, use a line JUST for it starting with \"@\", above the card (never on the same line). Each blank in the same card uses a different number (c1, c2...). In the explanation, one idea per \"+\" line, starting with the term followed by \" — \". The whole answer stays on one line (items separated by \" / \"); no markdown.",
  "help_text": "EASYANKICARDS — HOW TO USE\n\n1) PASTE YOUR TEXT (left panel)\n   One card per line:  Question :: Answer :: tags\n   • Separator: \"::\". The 3rd field (tags) is optional.\n   • Lines starting with \"#\" are ignored.\n   • HTML allowed: <b>bold</b>, <i>italic</i>.\n\n2) CLOZE CARDS\n   The capital of France is {{c1::Paris}}.\n   • c1, c2... create different blanks in the same sentence.\n   • Extra back and tags: Text {{c1::x}} :: Note :: tag\n\n3) PASTING FROM PDF / WORD / AI\n   The app tolerates line breaks in the middle of a card and\n   reorganizes shifted fields. To be safe, leave a BLANK LINE\n   between cards. Suspicious cards turn ORANGE with the\n   reason. \"Normalize text\" rewrites the editor in the\n   correct format.\n\n4) AUTOMATIC PREVIEW (right panel)\n   Updates as you type. Green = ok; orange = check.\n   Untick \"include\" to keep a card out of the export.\n\n5) DECK, SUBFOLDERS AND TAGS\n   • \"::\" in the deck name creates FOLDERS in Anki:\n     Bar Exam 2025::Administrative Law::Case Law\n     → cards land in the \"Case Law\" folder.\n     The destination shows in real time below the field.\n   • \"Copy path\": reuse the path on future exports and the\n     import drops cards straight into the right folder.\n   • The FILE NAME (.apkg or .txt) is just a label: the\n     destination is stored INSIDE the file, via the Deck field.\n     Renaming the file does NOT change the import folder.\n     Avoid the reserved name \"collection\".\n\n6) EXPORT\n   • .apkg (recommended): double-click and Anki imports it.\n     Same deck name = updates, no duplicates.\n   • .txt: Anki > File > Import (pre-configured).\n\n7) GENERATING CARDS WITH AI\n   • ChatGPT / Claude / Gemini: \"Copy full prompt\".\n   • Gemini Notebook (rejects long prompts): \"Copy short prompt\".\n   Paste the AI's reply straight into the editor.",
